<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 469)</h2>
<p><b>Optimised session bundles — one folder you can send.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>File ▸ Export Optimised Session Bundle…</b> puts the session, light stand-ins and their metadata in a single directory. Everything inside it is <b>relative</b>, so it plays on a machine that has never seen your media and carries no paths that only make sense on yours.</li>
<li><b>It finds its way home.</b> Each shot remembers where it came from, so a recipient who does have the original media opens the bundle straight onto it — and anyone who doesn't is told they're watching stand-ins.</li>
<li><b>Frame numbers survive the trip.</b> A render numbered 993–1042 reads 993–1042 inside the bundle, in the viewer and in burn-ins.</li>
<li>A stand-in now describes itself wherever it's opened, so the viewer, grabs and exports all agree about its numbering and colour without being told.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
